# Copper Linux -- the components startxfce offers before it starts the desktop.
#
# Three whitespace-separated columns:
#
#   <name>   <probe>                       <how>
#
# <probe> is a path that exists when the component is present. startxfce
# installs the missing ones whose <how> is "ingot", by asking ingot for them.
# <how> of "image" means the gui stage already ships it in the ISO: it is kept
# in this list so the report is honest about what a desktop is supposed to
# have, but ingot has no such package and startxfce will not try to install
# one -- a missing "image" component is a broken image, said out loud.
#
# The prompt names firefox and thunar as examples. Thunar and the terminal are
# "image": the gui stage installs xfce4, which pulls thunar, and build.sh names
# xfce4-terminal explicitly. Everything with "ingot" here is a payload in
# copper-ingot-repo (payloads-v1) carrying its own dependency closure.
firefox            /usr/bin/firefox            ingot
mousepad           /usr/bin/mousepad           ingot
ristretto          /usr/bin/ristretto          ingot
xfce4-taskmanager  /usr/bin/xfce4-taskmanager  ingot
xarchiver          /usr/bin/xarchiver          ingot
thunar             /usr/bin/thunar             image
xfce4-terminal     /usr/bin/xfce4-terminal     image
